   "id": "3-first-order-rl-and-rc-dc-transients",
   "title": "3. First-Order RL and RC DC Transients",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "3.1 The Universal Master Step Response Formula"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Valid for **ANY** voltage, current, or branch variable $x(t)$ in a stable first-order network:"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\mathbf{x(t) = x(\\infty) + \\Big[x(0^+) - x(\\infty)\\Big] e^{-t/\\tau}, \\quad t \\ge 0}"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "3.2 The 3-Pillar Solution Method"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "To solve any first-order transient problem:"
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "start": 1,
     "items": [
      "**Initial State $x(0^+)$**: Replace inductors with DC current sources $i_L(0^-)$ and capacitors with DC voltage sources $v_C(0^-)$. Solve the resulting resistive network for $x(0^+)$.",
      "**Final Steady State $x(\\infty)$**: Replace inductors with short circuits ($v_L = 0$) and capacitors with open circuits ($i_C = 0$). Solve for $x(\\infty)$.",
      "**Equivalent Time Constant $\\tau$**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\mathbf{\\tau_{RL} = \\frac{L}{R_{\\text{th}}}}, \\qquad \\mathbf{\\tau_{RC} = R_{\\text{th}} C}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "where $R_{\\text{th}}$ is the Thevenin equivalent resistance seen looking into the terminals of the storage element with **ALL independent sources deactivated**."
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "3.3 Key Time Constant Benchmarks"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**$t = \\tau$**: Variable completes **$63.2\\%$** of the total transition:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "x(\\tau) = x(\\infty) + [x(0^+) - x(\\infty)]e^{-1} = x(\\infty) + 0.368[x(0^+) - x(\\infty)]"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**$t = 2\\tau$**: Completes **$86.5\\%$** ($e^{-2} \\approx 0.135$).",
      "**$t = 3\\tau$**: Completes **$95.0\\%$** ($e^{-3} \\approx 0.050$).",
      "**$t = 4\\tau$**: Completes **$98.2\\%$** ($e^{-4} \\approx 0.018$).",
      "**$t = 5\\tau$**: Completes **$99.3\\%$** ($\\approx \\mathbf{\\text{Practical DC Steady State / Settling Time}}$).",
      "**Geometric Tangent Property**: The tangent line drawn to $x(t)$ at $t = 0^+$ intercepts the final steady-state horizontal asymptote at exactly $t = \\tau$."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "3.4 Multi-Interval Sequential Switching"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "When switches operate at different time instants ($t = 0$ and $t = t_1$):"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Interval 1 ($0 \\le t < t_1$)**: Use initial state $x(0^+)$ and time constant $\\tau_1$.",
      "**State Handoff at $t = t_1$**: Compute $x(t_1^-)$ from the Interval 1 equation. By continuity:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "i_L(t_1^+) = i_L(t_1^-), \\qquad v_C(t_1^+) = v_C(t_1^-)"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Interval 2 ($t \\ge t_1$)**: Time variable shifts to $(t - t_1)$:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "x(t) = x(\\infty) + \\Big[x(t_1^+) - x(\\infty)\\Big] e^{-(t - t_1)/\\tau_2}, \\quad t \\ge t_1"
    }
   ]
