   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "4.1 Singularity Relations"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\delta(t) = \\frac{du(t)}{dt}, \\quad u(t) = \\frac{dr(t)}{dt}, \\quad \\int_{0^-}^{0^+} \\delta(t)dt = 1"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "Step response $s(t)$ and impulse response $h(t)$:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "h(t) = \\frac{d s(t)}{dt}"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "4.2 Jump Discontinuities Under Impulse $\\delta(t)$ Excitation"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Inductor Current Jump**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\Delta i_L = i_L(0^+) - i_L(0^-) = \\frac{1}{L}\\int_{0^-}^{0^+} v_L(t)dt = \\mathbf{\\frac{\\text{Impulse Voltage Area}}{L}}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Capacitor Voltage Jump**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\Delta v_C = v_C(0^+) - v_C(0^-) = \\frac{1}{C}\\int_{0^-}^{0^+} i_C(t)dt = \\mathbf{\\frac{\\text{Impulse Current Area}}{C}}"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "4.3 Degenerate Capacitive Loops ($R = 0$) & Energy Paradox"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "When two capacitors are connected in a loop without series resistance across a step voltage $V$:"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "Loop resistance $R \\to 0 \\implies \\tau \\to 0$. An **infinite Dirac current impulse** $i(t) = \\Delta q \\cdot \\delta(t)$ flows.",
      "**Conservation of Charge**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "q_{\\text{loop}} = C_{\\text{eq}} \\Delta V = \\frac{C_1 C_2}{C_1 + C_2}[V - (V_1 + V_2)]"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Terminal Voltages at $t = 0^+$**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\mathbf{v_{C1}(0^+) = V_1 + [V - (V_1 + V_2)] \\frac{C_2}{C_1 + C_2}}, \\qquad \\mathbf{v_{C2}(0^+) = V_2 + [V - (V_1 + V_2)] \\frac{C_1}{C_1 + C_2}}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Energy Dissipation Paradox**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\Delta \\mathcal{E} = \\frac{1}{2} \\frac{C_1 C_2}{C_1 + C_2} [V - (V_1 + V_2)]^2"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "*This energy is dissipated as an electromagnetic spark/radiation in the switch regardless of how small $R$ is!*"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "4.4 Degenerate Inductive Cutsets / Loops"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Conservation of Flux Linkage**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\sum \\lambda(0^+) = \\sum \\lambda(0^-) \\iff L_1 i_1(0^+) + L_2 i_2(0^+) = L_1 i_1(0^-) + L_2 i_2(0^-)"
    }
   ]
