     "text": " 1. Overdamped (\u03b6 > 1  \u27fa  \u03b1 > \u03c9\u2080):\n    Roots: Two real, distinct negative roots (s_1 \u2260 s_2 < 0).\n    Response: Sluggish double-exponential decay without oscillations:\n              x(t) = A_1 e^{s_1 t} + A_2 e^{s_2 t}.\n \n 2. Critically Damped (\u03b6 = 1  \u27fa  \u03b1 = \u03c9\u2080):\n    Roots: Two real, equal negative roots (s_1 = s_2 = -\u03b1).\n    Response: Fastest non-oscillatory return to equilibrium:\n              x(t) = (A_1 + A_2 t) e^{-\u03b1 t}.\n \n 3. Underdamped (0 < \u03b6 < 1  \u27fa  \u03b1 < \u03c9\u2080):\n    Roots: Complex conjugate pair in Left Half Plane:  s_1,2 = -\u03b1 \u00b1 j \u03c9_d.\n    Damped Frequency:  \u03c9_d = \u221a(\u03c9\u2080\u00b2 - \u03b1\u00b2) = \u03c9\u2080 \u221a(1 - \u03b6\u00b2).\n    Response: Oscillatory ringing inside an exponentially decaying envelope:\n              x(t) = e^{-\u03b1 t} [ B_1 cos(\u03c9_d t) + B_2 sin(\u03c9_d t) ].\n \n 4. Undamped (\u03b6 = 0  \u27fa  \u03b1 = 0, R = 0 in series or R = \u221e in parallel):\n    Roots: Pure imaginary pair on j\u03c9-axis:  s_1,2 = \u00b1 j \u03c9\u2080.\n    Response: Sustained sinusoidal oscillation at frequency \u03c9\u2080:\n              x(t) = B_1 cos(\u03c9\u2080 t) + B_2 sin(\u03c9\u2080 t)."
